#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""L6.3.2.4 universal scheduler: validation-integrity hardening plus executed late-phase optimization.

The original ten-point structural scope is the foundation of this branch:
contract validation, deterministic pre-solver feasibility diagnostics, run and
contract identity hashes, stale-output protection, one canonical evaluator,
checkpoint/resume with tested-combination skipping, atomic verified publication,
instruction-driven break windows, transaction-safe repairs, and structural
blank/day-tail/overnight/cyclic audits. Result-driven selector, Pareto export,
and target-lock recovery improvements are layered on top rather than replacing
that baseline.

One instruction-driven engine supports all bundled and production workbooks;
client/case names are regression labels only. No client, roster size, associate
name, language name, interval count, or shift label is hard-coded.

Solve order
-----------
1. Parse and validate the workbook contract.
2. Run one hard-feasibility shift/OFF probe.
3. If hard-infeasible, run constraint-family isolation probes and stop.
4. If feasible, build target/floor/Pareto shift skeleton candidates.
5. Diagnose the minimum no-break requirement with certified lower/upper bounds.
6. Apply bounded shift/OFF repairs around break-conflict cells.
7. Convert certified exception bottlenecks into staffing-reserve constraints and run paired/multi-cell zero-exception recovery.
8. Retain compliant, near-feasible, and exception candidates in separate pools; near-feasible candidates are repair-only.
9. Assign exact break templates with progressive widening.
10. Only when explicitly permitted, use audited no-break associate-day exceptions.
11. Run generalized post-break shift/OFF repair and target-lock recovery while meaningful budget remains.
12. Prove selected exceptions, retain nondominated candidates, rebuild audits,
    and apply final release gates.
"""
